Setting (from the previous page). k is a field of characteristic 0, and X is a curve of type (g,ν) over k with a point x. These give geometric points ξ of M_{g,ν,Q} and x of the universal curve 𝔛_{g,ν,Q}. One then has the diagram of exact sequences (1): π_{X,x} = π_1(X,x) ⊂ 𝔊_{X,x} = π_1(𝔛_{g,ν,k̄}, x) ⊂ M_{X,x} = π_1(𝔛_{g,ν,Q}, x). There are quotients 𝔗_X = π_1(M_{g,ν,k̄}, ξ), N_X = π_1(M_{g,ν,Q}, ξ) and Γ_{Q̄/Q}. The 'standard' copies π̂_{g,ν}, 𝔊̂_{g,ν}, 𝔗̂_{g,ν}, M_{g,ν}, N_{g,ν} are defined the same way using a reference pair (X_0,x_0) over C.

This page: base-point change for the arithmetic Teichmüller tower.
- The (classes of étale) paths from the reference geometric point x_0 to x on the stack 𝔛_{g,ν,Q} form P_{X,x}, a right torsor under M_{g,ν}. The group M_{X,x} acts on it from the left, commuting with the right action, so P_{X,x} is a bitorsor.
- The whole diagram (1) at (X,x) is obtained from the standard diagram (1_{g,ν}) by contracted product P_{X,x} ∧^{M_{g,ν}} (–). Here M_{g,ν} acts on itself by inner automorphisms, and this action respects the filtration 1 ⊂ π̂ ⊂ 𝔊̂ ⊂ M (the subgroups are normal).
- The resulting list (4):
  - π_{X,x} = P ∧ π̂_{g,ν};
  - 𝔊_{X,x} = P ∧ 𝔊̂_{g,ν};
  - 𝔗_X = P ∧ 𝔗̂ = Q_X ∧^{N} 𝔗̂;
  - M_{X,x} = P ∧ M_{g,ν}, the inner twist, which is Aut(P);
  - N_X = P ∧ N = Q_X ∧ N;
  - Q̃ = P ∧ Q̄ = Q_X ∧ Q̄ = R ∧^{Γ} Q̄.
- On the next page Q_X = P ∧^{M} N_{g,ν} is the path torsor on the moduli stack, and R = P ∧^{M} Γ is the torsor of isomorphisms between the algebraic closure of Q in C and the algebraic closure Q̃ of Q in k.

Purpose: package the entire 'arithmetic fundamental group' data attached to a pointed curve over an arbitrary field k as one M_{g,ν}-torsor. The next page asks how much of (X,x) this torsor remembers, and finds it does not suffice. Its automorphism group M_{X,x} is uncountable, while Aut(X,x) over k is finite. This motivates passing to finitely generated subfields K_i of k, a Galois-theoretic (anabelian) characterization of points of moduli.
